{"chunk_id": "859206cddf5b", "text": "Rama, torn by duty and public opinion, orders Lakshmana to take the pregnant Sita away from Ayodhya and abandon her beyond the Ganges near the hermitage of the sage Valmiki. He forbids argument and insists the command be carried out immediately, even swearing that anyone who tries to change his decision will be treated as an enemy. Lakshmana, grief\u2011stricken but obedient, prepares a luxurious chariot with the charioteer Sumantra and tells Sita they are fulfilling her earlier wish to visit the forest hermitages by the Ganges. Delighted, Sita gathers jewels and garments to give to ascetics\u2019 wives. As they travel, however, she begins to sense ominous signs\u2014twitching eye, trembling limbs, and a growing unease\u2014while Lakshmana hides his anguish. The journey toward the Ganges quietly sets the stage for one of the epic\u2019s most tragic separations.\nRama orders Lakshmana to secretly leave Sita near Valmiki\u2019s hermitage, and Lakshmana sorrowfully takes her toward the Ganges while hiding the truth.\nThemes: duty versus compassion, exile of Sita, royal obedience, omens and foreboding, sacrifice", "vector": [0.01802387274801731, -0.02171829156577587, -0.011246244423091412, 0.017602818086743355, -0.02628198452293873, 0.012061189860105515, -0.0309950839728117, -0.009901585057377815, -0.013962728902697563, -0.02341609261929989, 0.021935610100626945, 0.014492442831397057, 0.003149423748254776, 0.019124047830700874, 0.004764033947139978, 0.0017283631023019552, 0.048027440905570984, -0.001804764149710536, 0.03455367684364319, -0.005942309275269508, -0.001803066348657012, -0.018444927409291267, 0.007809891831129789, 0.008923650719225407, -0.029636841267347336, -0.010084947571158409, 0.01604083925485611, -0.026186907663941383, 0.012292090803384781, -0.02158246748149395, -0.013290398754179478, -0.021663961932063103, -0.01693727821111679, -0.01285576168447733, -0.038220930844545364, 0.009507694281637669, -0.002587451133877039